One of "the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World," the Colossus of Rhodes depicted the sun god Helios. It stood at an impressive 108 ft high (according to most contemporary descriptions), making it the tallest statue of the ancient world. It was destroyed in an earthquake in 226 BCE, so you are lucky to be seeing it. Thank you time travel! Though it is a wonder, it is not the solution to this maze of spacetime.